{
  "id": "COMPOUND:22032 - PROTEIN:5790",
  "verbalization": "Jatamanin C is implicated in the target engagement of HPAC through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Jatamanin C directly targets SNU-387, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside and 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. These compounds all ultimately have HPAC as their target. This chain of targets implies a potential pathway where Jatamanin C may influence HPAC through the activation of these downstream molecules. The presence of multiple overlapping targets further supports the idea that Jatamanin C may act as a modulator or activator of the signaling pathways involving HPAC. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, emphasizing the role of SNU-387 as a central mediator in the interaction between Jatamanin C and HPAC.",
